questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where an order fulfillment service silently fails to process tasks asynchronously and fails to isolate transaction rollbacks. A code review reveals the following Spring Service implementation:

java
@Service
public class OrderFulfillmentService {

    public void dispatchOrders(List<Order> orders) {
        for (Order order : orders) {
            processOrder(order);
        }
    }

    @Async
    @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
    public void processOrder(Order order) {
        // update inventory and charge payment
        order.setStatus(OrderStatus.PROCESSED);
    }
}


During high-load incidents, calling `dispatchOrders` blocks the main request thread and partial failures leave database records in an inconsistent state.
